          "text": "**Analyzing event handling**\n\nI'm looking at how the event store is set up to manage a maximum of 50 events and how it might silently discard older ones, which raises concerns about operational loss. It's possible that this was designed intentionally. \n\nThen, there's an issue with the ErrorHandler where clicking on the link navigates the browser, likely due to how preventDefault isn't enabled. The ErrorBoundary behavior seems to expose a stack to the user, which poses both operational and security risks. \n\nAlso, I noticed that the report filter might have an issue with device IDs being treated as strings instead of numbers, which could confuse the API.",
